# Testing

Vitest for unit and integration. Testcontainers with **real MySQL** for anything touching the database. Playwright for end-to-end and accessibility.

## Never test the database against a substitute

The tenancy guard is the thing most worth testing and the thing an in-memory or SQLite substitute will not exercise faithfully. Integration tests run against real MySQL via Testcontainers.

## Suites that block the build

| Suite | What it proves |
|---|---|
| `test/tenancy/` | No cross-tenant read, write, update, delete or list leak (`FR-TEN-010`) |
| `test/money/` | Exact decimal arithmetic, rounding at the specified points, FX applied once, voucher allocation reconciles |
| `test/contract/` | Responses conform to the published OpenAPI spec |
| `test/authz/` | Default deny; explicit deny beats grant; permissions in one OEM never affect another |

None of these are skipped, quarantined, or marked flaky-tolerant. If one is failing, it is telling the truth.

## Writing tests

- Tests describe behaviour, not implementation. Renaming a private method must not break a test.
- One assertion subject per test. A test that asserts five unrelated things reports one failure for five problems.
- Use the BRD's acceptance criteria as test names where they exist — `AC-ORD-001-01` is a test name.
- Fixtures create **two tenants by default**, so a cross-tenant mistake fails immediately rather than in a dedicated suite six months later.
- No `.only` on a committed test. The linter should reject it.

## Money tests

Transcribe the worked examples from BRD Parts 5 and 6 before implementing the pricing engine. Include:

- A voucher allocated across lines with different VAT rates, where the allocation has a rounding remainder
- A price authored in EUR, displayed in GBP, with conversion applied once
- A page-priced product at minimum, at an increment boundary, and above maximum

## Accessibility tests

Playwright + axe on every admin screen, in the pipeline, not only before release. An accessibility regression is a build failure. (`FR-SCP-007`)

## What not to test

Do not test framework behaviour, generated code, or the ORM. Test your rules.
